Keyboard rotation QTE guide, after a live run of the cabin minigame (issue 34 follow-up). The guide took its keys from
the drawn arrow matrix: the arrows animate (the matrix rotates, so issue 34 showed S > D > W), and each 360 / Down180CCW
diagram draws two leaves with opposite windings, so the guide and the keyboard sweep flipped between clockwise and
counter-clockwise every frame and the game rejected the turn. The gesture now comes from the exported symbol name
(zzz-317 instance ancestry), which matched every observed single-leaf winding, and guides are short so the timing is
reachable: half turns start > end (Down180CW D > A, Down180CCW A > D, Up180CW A > D, Up180CCW D > A) with an explicit
turn that makes the sweep pass under the bottom or over the top. Full turns are one held key: W > S > W was still too slow
for the prompt's window in the live run, so while W is held the stick turns the prompt's way at two turns per second
(like the opt-in Circle gesture) and stops on release; the key shows a circular arrow of that direction.
GOW_ICONOS_DIAG=1 logs [gow-qte-guide] (symbol, matrix, guide, turn) when they change. Tests: control-prompts,
qte_hold_test.

